 "text": "9/29/26, 9:48 AM\nThe corresponding data elements in SAP S/4HANA are:\n\ne Items: OPBEL + OPUPW + OPUPK\n\ne Splitltems: OPUPZ\n\nNote that in the FI-CA backend a cleared Splitltem always points to its clearing document, whereas in the message structure the\ncleared Splitltem always points to the payment or credit memo that cleared it.\n\nMessage Types\n\ne ContractAccountERPReceivablesPayablesRegisterltemBylDQuery_sync\n\ne ContractAccountERPReceivablesPayablesRegisterltemBylDResponse_sync\n\nConstraints\n\nIn case invoices have been partially cleared by payments in other currencies, errors may occur when you display the partial\namounts of the invoices.\n\nNotes on SAP Implementation\nPrerequisites\nYou are using software component FI-CA (as of version FI-CA 6.02).\n\nYou have maintained the backend configuration of SAP Biller Direct in FI-CA (see Customizing for Contract Accounts Receivable\nand Payable under Integration -> Financial Supply Chain Management -> Biller Direct -> Basic Setting for Customer Portal in\nInternet ).\n\nThe user has sufficient authorizations, in particular with regard to the authorization object F_KK_EBPP.\nProcessing\n\nFI-CA event 6607 is called directly after inbound mapping of the service is done; it can be used to modify the query fields before\nthe business logic is performed.\n\nFI-CA event 6608 is called before the response message is returned to the service consumer; it can be used to modify the\nresponse fields and to handle customer extensions carried out in the service interface\n\nFI-CA event 6600 can be used to map an external contract account ID to the internal contract account ID.\n\nMore Information\n\nFor information on corrections and frequently asked questions relating to this operation, refer to SAP Note 1063631 (collective\nnote).\n\nFind Contract Account Split Item Group by Business Partner ID\n",
